1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,157
Live commentary moves too fast to check.

2
00:00:03,207 --> 00:00:05,991
Say one wrong number, and it is on air.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:12,908
A claim, in English or Vietnamese, gets a verdict from the rules in under a second,

4
00:00:08,024 --> 00:00:14,524
“Đội nhà áp đảo hiệp 2” = “The home side dominated the second half”

5
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:15,362
with the numbers and events behind it.

6
00:00:15,412 --> 00:00:19,429
An open model on the same small CPU then writes an explanation,

7
00:00:19,479 --> 00:00:21,237
and the guardrail checks it.

8
00:00:21,287 --> 00:00:25,240
Here it refused the model's text, so the rules' answer stands.

9
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:34,456
Fourteen agents on Microsoft Agent Framework share one match state and hand off typed messages.

10
00:00:34,506 --> 00:00:36,984
Agent Ops shows every handoff, live.

11
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:39,587
Break the model yourself.

12
00:00:39,637 --> 00:00:42,924
Here it lies: valid answers with one number changed.

13
00:00:42,974 --> 00:00:47,351
The guardrail blocks every one, and nothing wrong reaches the screen.

14
00:00:52,033 --> 00:00:56,174
At every key moment the studio gets verified talking points,

15
00:00:56,224 --> 00:00:59,247
and an on-air graphic ready for OBS or vMix.

16
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:08,966
For fans everywhere, commentary in their own language: here Vietnamese, read aloud,

17
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:10,833
Fan view: casual · Vietnamese · a Kestrel fan · beginner mode

18
00:01:09,016 --> 00:01:13,525
with a beginner mode that explains offside the first time it happens.

19
00:01:14,213 --> 00:01:16,363
M. Ribas is caught offside.

20
00:01:16,413 --> 00:01:18,034
Offside: An attacker is offside when, in the opponents' half,

21
00:01:18,084 --> 00:01:21,293
they are nearer the goal line than both the ball and the second-last defender at the moment a team-mate plays the ball,

22
00:01:21,343 --> 00:01:22,493
and they become involved in play.

23
00:01:22,543 --> 00:01:24,410
There is no offside directly from a throw-in, a corner or a goal kick.

24
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:25,669
The defending team gets an indirect free kick.

25
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,708
The same statistics are served over MCP to any AI assistant.

26
00:01:30,758 --> 00:01:36,313
The whole stack runs in one CPU container with an open model: no cloud account,

27
00:01:36,363 --> 00:01:38,726
the data never leaves the machine.

28
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:44,590
Pundit Copilot: never wrong on air.

29
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,156
Synthetic data only.
